WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.920
Some were highly anticipated, some looked
intriguing on the surface but failed to deliver,

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.880
and some struggled to even make the public
aware of their existence, but they all have

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.620
one thing in common: they tanked badly at
the box office.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.160
Based on a notoriously dangerous real-life
New Jersey theme park, Action Point starred

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.020
Johnny Knoxville of Jackass fame as the irresponsible
owner of the most dangerous vacation spot

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:23.780
in America.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.320
Featuring plenty of actual, life-and-limb
threatening stunts from its seasoned performers,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.640
Action Point promised lowbrow belly laughs
along the lines of the Jackass film series.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.800
There was only one problem: the movie's awful.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.060
Fans found the theme park narrative to be
awkwardly grafted onto what could easily have

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.780
just been another Jackass movie.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.480
Even though Knoxville practically killed himself
making the movie, the stunts were also seen

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.380
as uninspired and the laughs were few and
far between.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.080
Despite the premise and the pedigree to be
a potential horror classic, Winchester was

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.300
just a disappointment.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.579
Dame Helen Mirren starred as Sarah Winchester,
heiress to the gun manufacturer's fortune,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.080
who spent decades building strange additions
onto her famous mansion.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.660
The film posited that her bizarre architecture
choices were driven by something decidedly

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.660
supernatural

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:13.039
Unfortunately, Winchester relies on cheap
jump scares and questionable plotting in lieu

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.350
of anything resembling atmosphere or tension.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.639
"I trust everything has been to your satisfaction
so far?"

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.479
"I cannot fault the hospitality."

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.280
"it's quite a special house, is it not?"

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:28.300
The John Travolta biopic Gotti got a lot of
press due to its star and subject, infamous

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.820
mob boss John Gotti, leading up to its screening
at Cannes.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:35.740
But its reception at the festival was less
than rapturous, and upon its June release

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.080
in the U.S., few critics bothered to review
it.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:42.770
Literally every single one that did panned
it — leading the film's social media account

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.280
to pin its subsequent poor box office showing
on unfair negative reviews.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.560
Literally every aspect of the film's production
was roundly blasted, from its lack of coherent

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.300
themes and ham-fisted direction to Travolta's
terrible lead performance.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.960
The movie failed to even make back half of
its paltry $10 million budget, which is a

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.660
sure sign of movie failure.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:06.859
A futuristic sci-fi thriller with a cast most
directors would kill for didn't stop Hotel

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.760
Artemis from completely tanking at the box
office.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:14.239
Part of the problem was that director Drew
Pearce's preference for style over substance

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:16.550
resulted in a great premise falling flat.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:21.280
Worse, the film's marketing, largely free
of plot or character details, did nothing

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.400
to pull audiences in.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.870
Those willing to take the plunge were met
with a convoluted plot laced with laborious,

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.700
needlessly expository dialogue.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.920
Despite its modest $15 million budget, Hotel
Artemis didn't even crack half that at the

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:39.080
domestic box office as any good hotel owner
will tell you, you just can't turn a profit

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.560
with that kind of vacancy rate.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.580
The Darkest Minds seemed to come with a built-in
audience.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.819
It's an adaptation of the well-received young
adult novel of the same name and features

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.200
superpowered characters that could have come
straight from the latest X-Men movie.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.099
Unfortunately, critics took the film to task
for being muddled, confusing and trite and

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:01.040
it whiffed with audiences as well, failing
to even clear $6 million in its opening weekend.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.440
Many critics felt that Minds is guilty of
pandering to its audience, giving them a predictable

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.510
story full of tired cliches and obvious plot
twists.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.060
In the case of The Darkest Minds, it seems
like assembling rehashed plot points from

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.720
better movies wasn't enough to get audiences
to care.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:20.400
Many critics thought that Alpha would be a
welcome return to form for Albert Hughes,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.400
who was partly responsible for the classic
hard-boiled crime pictures Menace II Society

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.540
and Dead Presidents.

00:03:26.129 --> 00:03:30.540
Alpha tells the story of a prehistoric youth
who becomes separated from his hunting group,

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.280
and in order to survive, partners up with
a lone wolf abandoned by its pack.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:38.891
It's a thrilling, gorgeously-shot adventure,
but while the film scored with critics, it

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.520
failed to connect with audiences.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.859
With an advertising campaign which seemed
to be aimed more squarely at dog lovers than

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:49.329
fans of epic adventure, Alpha simply didn't
generate the kind of positive word of mouth

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.020
that it needed.

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:54.600
It also had the misfortune of squaring off
against Crazy Rich Asians and The Meg, two

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.100
films which destroyed at the box office.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:01.790
Alpha failed to make back its budget domestically,
but it seems destined for a robust second

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.980
life on home video.

